# Copy to .env and fill in. .env is gitignored; this file is not.
# The key NEVER goes in the plist, in a script, or in a commit.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#   $EDITOR .env
#   ./scripts/morning.sh --dry-run     # must print extractor=ai
#
# Rotating it? Two places, both or neither:
#   1. this file, on the Mac
#   2. the GitHub repo secret GROQ_API_KEY
# Update one and not the other and that half falls back to the free extractive
# path — quietly. morning.sh warns when the Mac half drifts; the podcasts
# workflow warns when the CI half does.

# Groq free tier — https://console.groq.com/keys
GROQ_API_KEY=

# Optional. Anthropic instead of Groq, ~$0.50 an episode. Groq wins when both
# are set; AI_PROVIDER overrides.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# Optional. Force a mode instead of inferring it from which keys are present.
# EXTRACTOR=local makes the free path deliberate and silences the downgrade
# warning.
# EXTRACTOR=local

# ── YOUTUBE CAPTIONS ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Signed-out caption requests are answered with HTTP 429 from a home IP and
# "Sign in to confirm you're not a bot" from CI. Measured 2026-09-19: the same
# video went from a 2-second 429 to a full transcript with Safari's cookies.
# safari | chrome — leave EMPTY in CI, which has no browser.
YTDLP_COOKIES_FROM_BROWSER=
# An exported cookies.txt instead, for a process that cannot read the browser
# database (a launchd job without Full Disk Access). Takes precedence.
YTDLP_COOKIES_FILE=
